  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Budget and Financial Accountability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance is focused on assisting the Accountant General with the publication of financial statements to conform to the requirements of the International Public Sector Accounting Standards (IPSAS), and the Office of Contracting and Procurement Policy with the implementation of a purchasing card program and the a cooperative purchasing agreement. The IPSAS A includes: assisting in the preparation of year-end financial statements that are in compliance with international accounting standards for central administration and other government entities; reviewing laws and regulations and recommending changes to the legislative framework; developing regulations and manuals including procedures to gather data and templates for reporting formats and the notes to financial statements; providing training to Accountant General and staff as well as training materials to be used by Accountant General to train other institutions; reviewing functionality of the automated accounting system (SIAFI) and identifying changes needed to serve as the primary source of financial information throughout the Finance Ministry; and reviewing SIAFI functionality to meet the needs of the controlled institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
